Deploy the solution through controlled development, testing, and production environments. Each stage should produce a validated output before the solution advances to the next stage.

Deployment Steps

Develop and validate Snowflake curated views and tables in the approved development environment.

Configure Power BI connections and implement Power Query transformations.

Build fact and dimension tables and validate the star-schema relationships.

Mark DimDate as the date table and test date-based calculations.

Create DAX measures and reconcile KPI results with Snowflake.

Build report pages, slicers, drill-through navigation, and visual interactions.

Configure dynamic RLS and test representative user-access scenarios.

Publish the semantic model and report to the development workspace and validate the published behavior.

Configure the approved Snowflake cloud connection, credentials, permissions, and scheduled refresh for Import models. Validate connectivity and refresh behavior for the selected storage mode.

Complete user acceptance testing, document approval, and promote the solution through Test to Production using the organization's controlled deployment process.

After production deployment, verify report access, refresh status, security assignments, and key KPI totals. Establish an operational process for monitoring failures and managing subsequent model changes.

